  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive). Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{盗|ぬす}む (steal X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates completed action. {盗|ぬす}んでいる = 'has stolen.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{物|もの}→物：02259_mono⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{盗|ぬす}む (steal things)\n- {盗|ぬす}まれる (be stolen—passive, very common)\n- ⟦こっそり→こっそり：05890_kossori⟧{盗|ぬす}む (steal stealthily)\n- {盗|ぬす}み⟦{見|み}る→見る：00283_miru⟧ (peep, peek)\n- {盗|ぬす}み⟦{聞|ぎ}き→聞く：00483_kiku⟧ (eavesdropping)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{泥棒|どろぼう}→泥棒：01688_dorobou⟧ (thief, burglar)\n- ⟦{窃盗|せっとう}→窃盗：15280_settou⟧ (theft—formal/legal term)\n- ⟦{盗難|とうなん}→盗難：04562_tounan⟧ (theft, robbery—noun)\n\nPASSIVE USAGE: Victims often use the passive {盗|ぬす}まれる to describe their experience:\n- ⟦{自転車|じてんしゃ}→自転車：00633_jitensha⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{盗|ぬす}まれた (My bicycle was stolen)",
